# VFS491 fingerprint sensor (USB 138a:003d).
#
# Keep the sensor powered while it is plugged in.
#
# The kernel's default USB autosuspend delay is 2 seconds, and the VFS491's
# endpoints do not survive a suspend/resume cycle: a capture that spans one
# comes back truncated (a 200x86 or 200x58 strip instead of a 200x300 print),
# and repeated suspend/resume cycles eventually leave the device wedged so it
# stops opening at all.
#
# Disabling autosuspend for this one device keeps swipes full length and the
# sensor recoverable without a reboot. It is the only hardware-specific rule
# in this project, and it matches on the USB IDs rather than a bus port.
#
# The capture path uses HP's own tool, not a libfprint driver, so libfprint's
# own autosuspend hwdb (which deliberately *enables* suspend for known-good
# devices) does not apply here.

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="138a", ATTR{idProduct}=="003d", ATTR{power/control}="on"
